    {
      "id": 3002,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        -850.0100059475169,
        3761.30197118407
      ],
      "size": [
        524.1988313713744,
        475.77576076249306
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 6,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note",
        "ue_properties": {
          "version": "7.8",
          "widget_ue_connectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "SCAIL-2 EASY CONFIG + AUTO LOOP - QUICK GUIDE\n===============================================\n\nONE config node (top-left) + ONE auto node (this loop) control everything:\n\n  seconds  |  10 = only the first 10 s are animated (0 = whole video)\n  fps      |  16 = Wan native. 20/22/24 work too (more frames = more VRAM/time)\n  width/height | 0 = AUTO: use driving video resolution / keep aspect ratio\n  steps / cfg  | 6 / 1.0 = LightX2V distill defaults\n  seed     |  used for ALL segments when randomize is OFF\n  randomize_seed | ON: one NEW random seed per Queue run, shared by ALL segments\n  replace_mode | OFF = Animation (full reference image, ALL subjects animate)\n                ON = Replacement (only the tracked person is swapped)\n\nTHE LOOP NODE generates the video in 81-frame segments (76-frame steps, 5-frame\noverlap anchor) automatically and chains them until seconds x fps are reached:\n    5 s =  81 frames ->  1 segment\n   10 s = 160 frames ->  2 segments\n   15 s = 240 frames ->  4 segments\n   30 s = 480 frames ->  7 segments\nOutput is trimmed to EXACTLY seconds x fps frames (frozen tail only when the\nrequest goes past the driving video). Model is loaded once.\n\nCONSOLE LOG: every run prints the seed and the exact source-frame window used\nper chunk (e.g. \"drives source frames 76..156\") to the ComfyUI console/log.\n\nUNLIMITED / CONTINUE this video in a NEW run (pick up where it stopped):\n  1. set VHS_LoadVideo skip_first_frames = printed \"first unused source frame\" (e.g. 157),\n     keep seconds + frame_load_cap as-is\n  2. feed this run\"s last 5 OUTPUT frames into the loop node\"s \"anchor_frames\"\n     input (e.g. VHS_LoadVideo on the output mp4, frame_load_cap=5, take last 5)\n  3. Queue -> new run is anchored to the previous one, no jump at the seam\n\nNEW NODE - SCAIL-2 Run Info: add it from the node menu (category SCAIL-2), type the\noutput filename (e.g. SCAIL2_FULL_00001.mp4) and read seed / frames / fps / res /\nsteps / cfg / prompts / mode from its outputs, or preview the \"message\" output.\nWorks on VHS mp4s (metadata embedded via save_metadata) and ComfyUI PNGs.\n\nMASKS - IMPORTANT:\n- Keep the config node\"s \"object_indices\" EMPTY (\"\" = all people) or set \"0\" for\n  only the leftmost person. NEVER type True/False in it - it is a comma-separated\n  index list, not a toggle. Entering True/False makes SCAIL2ColoredMask select\n  ZERO objects -> empty masks -> the model receives no conditioning.\n- Both SAM3_VideoTrack nodes use max_objects=2 with sort_by=left_to_right so the\n  same person gets the same color in the pose mask and the reference mask.\n  With max_objects=1 the video tracker may pick the wrong person -> identity breaks.\n- Verify: preview the two SCAIL2ColoredMask outputs; the same color must land on\n  the same person in both.\n\nFRESH INSTALL: no code changes needed - copy custom_nodes/scail2-easy-config/ (pack\nREADME) + this workflow + models; see the repo README.md / INSTALL.md.\nMODELS - DOWNLOAD (6 files, ~15-20 GB total). No auto-download in this workflow;\ngrab them manually from these links, or run download_models.bat (Windows) /\ndownload_models.sh (Linux & macOS) from the repo root to fetch them automatically.\n\n 1. Diffusion model (GGUF, pick ONE) -> ComfyUI/models/unet/\n    - 12 GB VRAM: SCAIL-2-Q4_K_M.gguf (~10.9 GB)\n      https://huggingface.co/realrebelai/SCAIL-2_GGUF/resolve/main/SCAIL-2-Q4_K_M.gguf\n    - 8 GB VRAM:  SCAIL-2-Q3_K_M.gguf (~8.1 GB)\n      https://huggingface.co/realrebelai/SCAIL-2_GGUF/resolve/main/SCAIL-2-Q3_K_M.gguf\n 2. Text encoder umt5_xxl_fp8_e4m3fn_scaled.safetensors -> models/text_encoders/\n    https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Wan_2.1_ComfyUI_repackaged/resolve/main/split_files/text_encoders/umt5_xxl_fp8_e4m3fn_scaled.safetensors\n 3. SAM3 object tracker sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors -> models/checkpoints/\n    https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/sam3.1/resolve/main/checkpoints/sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors\n 4. CLIP vision clip_vision_h.safetensors -> models/clip_vision/\n    https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Wan_2.1_ComfyUI_repackaged/resolve/main/split_files/clip_vision/clip_vision_h.safetensors\n 5. VAE wan_2.1_vae.safetensors -> models/vae/\n    https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Wan_2.1_ComfyUI_repackaged/resolve/main/split_files/vae/wan_2.1_vae.safetensors\n 6. LightX2V distill LoRA Wan21_I2V_14B_lightx2v_cfg_step_distill_lora_rank64.safetensors -> models/loras/\n    https://huggingface.co/lightx2v/Wan2.1-I2V-14B-480P-StepDistill-CfgDistill-Lightx2v/resolve/main/loras/Wan21_I2V_14B_lightx2v_cfg_step_distill_lora_rank64.safetensors"
      ],
